- Assist in the innovation and transformation of the team’s workflows by managing the development and implementation of automation solutions using various tools and technologies;
- Compile various management reports on market performance;
- Support new business initiatives, new products, system & infrastructure enhancements, market microstructure improvement and other ad-hoc assignments as required. This involves: - Reviewing of policies, rules, procedures, and systems
- Coordinating and executing projects
- Liaising with statutory bodies, internal departments, and external business counterparties
- Providing user requirements and conducting User Acceptance Tests (UAT)
- Conducting research
Requirements:
- University Degree holder preferably in Finance/ Statistics/ Information Technology or related disciplines;
- Sound knowledge of the derivatives products, market practices and the trading platform;
- 2+ years’ relevant experience in finance/ equity trading business. High-calibre candidates with less experience will also be considered;
- Good communication and problem-solving skills;
- Good command of written and spoken English and Chinese, proficiency in Putonghua is an advantage;
- Proficient with MS Word, Excel and PowerPoint, knowledge in Power BI, SQL and VBA an advantage;
- Shift duties are required, and work experience with shift duties is an added advantage;
- High agility with growth mindset; a self-starter, team player and good communicator with sound judgment and good problem-solving skills.
- Shift duties are required, and work experience with shift duties is an added advantage
